						<div class="archive-awards-group__title">
							<h4>Jury’s Award</h4>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="archive-awards-group__cards">
						<article class="archive-awards-card">
							<img src="/assets/2025/awards/posters/2025-jury-award-1.png" alt="Life is Snow poster" loading="lazy" />
							<div class="archive-awards-card__content">
								<p class="archive-awards-card__eyebrow">Visual Innovation</p>
								<h5>Life is Snow</h5>
								<p class="archive-awards-card__body">
									Among this year’s submissions, we were delighted to discover a film
									that investigates the shifts between generations of migrants with
									classical narrative precision. The film draws power from its
									concentrated storytelling.
								</p>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article class="archive-awards-card">
							<img src="/assets/2025/awards/posters/2025-jury-award-2.jpg" alt="The First Photograph poster" loading="lazy" />
							<div class="archive-awards-card__content">
								<p class="archive-awards-card__eyebrow">Narrative Depth</p>
								<h5>The First Photograph</h5>
								<p class="archive-awards-card__body">
									An experimental short tracing a father’s exile and diaspora through
									archives, maps, and family album negatives. A brave journey
									questioning time, memory, and images.
								</p>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="archive-awards-group">
					<div class="archive-awards-group__header">
						<div class="archive-awards-group__title">
							<h4>Audience Choice Award</h4>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="archive-awards-group__cards">
						<article class="archive-awards-card">
							<img src="/assets/2025/awards/posters/2025-audience-award.jpg" alt="An Unfinished Film poster" loading="lazy" />
							<div class="archive-awards-card__content">
								<p class="archive-awards-card__eyebrow">Audience Choice Award</p>
								<h5>An Unfinished Film</h5>
								<p class="archive-awards-card__body">Ye Lou · Singapore, Germany</p>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="archive-awards-group">
					<div class="archive-awards-group__header">
						<div class="archive-awards-group__title">
							<h4>Special Mention</h4>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="archive-awards-group__cards">
						<article class="archive-awards-card">
							<img src="/assets/2025/awards/posters/2025-special-mention1.jpg" alt="Before Then (O Ma) poster" loading="lazy" />
							<div class="archive-awards-card__content">
								<p class="archive-awards-card__eyebrow">Visual Innovation</p>
								<h5>Before Then (O Ma)</h5>
								<p class="archive-awards-card__body">
									An intimately crafted autobiographical documentary layered with
									fragile recollections and a profound intergenerational bond.
								</p>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article class="archive-awards-card">
							<img src="/assets/2025/awards/posters/2025-special-mention2.jpg" alt="The Periphery of the Base poster" loading="lazy" />
							<div class="archive-awards-card__content">
								<p class="archive-awards-card__eyebrow">Narrative Depth</p>
								<h5>The Periphery of the Base</h5>
								<p class="archive-awards-card__body">
									A cinematic eye for the tension between monumental construction,
									harsh geography, and human fragility, pushing documentary language
									into abstracted registers of the real.
								</p>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<section class="archive-section" id="events-2025">
				<div class="archive-section__head">
					<h3>Special events</h3>
				</div>
				<div class="archive-events">
					<div class="archive-event">
						<div class="archive-event__media">
							<img src="/assets/2025/2025-event.jpg" alt="Event photo" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
						<div class="archive-event__content">
							<span class="archive-event__tag">In Between And Never There - No 1. - Chinese Diaspora in St. Pauli</span>
							<p><strong>Partner:</strong> Millerntorwache</p>
							<p><strong>Curator:</strong> Bettina Freimann</p>
							<p>
								In Between And Never There is an artistic activation of the
								Millerntorwache, curated by Bettina Freimann. The project opens with
								Nostalgia Machines, a video work by Hong Kong-based artist duo Zheng
								Mahler, which examines techno-orientalism, nostalgia, and speculative
								futures through the lens of identity, belonging, and geopolitical
								power shifts. Set within historic architecture, the immersive video
								installation creates a dynamic tension between forgotten past and
								speculative futures, between inside and outside.
							</p>
							<div class="archive-event__content-subsection">
								<h4 class="archive-event__subtitle">About the Curator</h4>
								<p>
									Bettina Freimann is currently the Project Director of the 9th
									Triennial of Photography Hamburg 2026. As an independent curator and
									Sinologist, she focuses on contemporary art from China and Asia, with
									a strong interest in transcultural perspectives. She has realized
									projects for CHINA TIME 2018 and 2022, India Week, and the
									Fotofestiwal Łódź. From 2016 to 2021, she co-curated the
									Hamburg-based art space Âme Nue. She has also developed and led
									cultural projects for the Confucius Institute Hamburg, the
									Goethe-Institut Beijing, and the Hamburg Ministry of Justice.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

